# P3.1: Multi-Vector APT Detection
#
# Formal Specification (MFOTL):
#   apt_indicator(d, t) ←
#     (◇[0,60] overflow(d) ∧ ◇[0,60] time_anomaly(d)) ∨
#     (◇[0,60] overflow(d) ∧ ◇[0,60] fuzzing(d)) ∨
#     (◇[0,60] time_anomaly(d) ∧ ◇[0,60] fuzzing(d))
#
# Equivalent (Mathematical Logic):
#   ∃t₁, t₂. (t-60 ≤ t₁ ≤ t) ∧ (t-60 ≤ t₂ ≤ t) ∧
#     ((overflow(d, t₁) ∧ time_anomaly(d, t₂)) ∨
#      (overflow(d, t₁) ∧ fuzzing(d, t₂)) ∨
#      (time_anomaly(d, t₁) ∧ fuzzing(d, t₂)))
#
# Semantics: Device d exhibits at least 2 different attack types
#            within 60 seconds → flag as APT indicator

# MonPoly formula (direct MFOTL with free variable d for output)
# Detects if device d shows 2+ different attack types within 60s
# Free variable d will appear in MonPoly output: @ts. (...): (device_name)
( (ONCE[0,60] overflow(d, _)) AND (ONCE[0,60] time_anomaly(d, _)) ) OR
( (ONCE[0,60] overflow(d, _)) AND (ONCE[0,60] fuzzing(d, _)) ) OR
( (ONCE[0,60] time_anomaly(d, _)) AND (ONCE[0,60] fuzzing(d, _)) )